YouHexen2 - a web-native Hexen II port
======================================

https://github.com/alextnewman/youhexen2

YouHexen2 is Hammer of Thyrion / uHexen2 rebuilt as an HTML5 game for an installed iOS PWA. The engine runs as WebAssembly and owns first-party browser backends for WebGPU rendering, WebAudio, input, persistent storage, lifecycle, and fullscreen play.

WebGlideNitro is the primary renderer. It preserves Hexen II's indexed textures, palette and colormap lighting, authored light styles, and crunchy software-rendered character while extending them with GPU-driven lighting and effects. The classic 8-bit software renderer remains available as the correctness reference and presents through WebGPU.

The supported target is an installed PWA on iPadOS. This tree no longer builds the inherited Linux, Windows, SDL, OpenGL, multiplayer, or dedicated-server products.

YouHexen2 does not include game data. Import pak0.pak and pak1.pak from a legally owned copy of Hexen II through the PWA launcher; import portals/pak3.pak for Portal of Praevus. Imported data and saves remain local to the browser and work offline.

